  "result_text": "**Recommendation: lean hold, unless you have a strong reason to think a real regression was very unlikely before looking at the data.** The data don't settle it, so the verdict is `prior-sensitive` and the final call comes back to you.\n\n**How I got there**\n- **Evidence:** The canary hosts' p95 gap is 57 ms against a 40 ms noise band. Past rollouts (S2) show the gap in 9 of 10 real regressions and 2 of 10 non-regressions. That is a likelihood ratio of 4.5, so seeing this gap makes a real regression 4.5 times more likely, in odds terms. I counted it once, since T1 and T3 are the same observation. The ratio comes from only 20 rollouts, and I treated it as a single number rather than a range.\n- **Loss threshold:** I took your \"roughly ten\" as 10 exactly, so holding is right once the odds of a real regression pass 1 to 10 (about 9%).\n- **Prior:** I couldn't set a prior. The S2 sample was drawn with fixed quotas, so it says nothing about how often a gap turns out to be real. I swept a range of priors instead.\n- **Crossover:** With a 4.5 ratio and a 10:1 loss, holding wins whenever your pre-evidence odds of a real regression exceed about 0.022, which is roughly 2%. Shipping only wins if you'd have put the chance of a real regression below about 2% before seeing the gap.\n- **Caveat:** That range is my choice, not data. In my swept range, a prior of 0.01 odds gives ship, and anything from 0.0222 up gives hold.\n\n**What would change this**\n- **H2 is untested.** Both ledger explanations are still open. The raw access logs (S3) would show whether the gap is real or an exporter artifact. A flat raw-log p95 would favor shipping, and a matching gap would confirm a real regression. The ledger says the logs are kept 7 days and a restore request is pending. They'd be dated 2026-09-09, so please check that the restore doesn't run out before Friday.\n- **Rollback cost:** You didn't give the cost of rolling back a shipped regression, and the 10x figure may already include it.\n- **Loss ratio:** If the true loss ratio were closer to 2, the answer would depend more heavily on the prior.\n\nThis is a recommendation only. It doesn't authorize the hold, the ship, or pulling the logs.\n\nThe full record is at `/var/folders/4_/s6fbcjyn4b13xdxkd3lv0kw00000gn/T/arm-w2-da-s1-post-ag_zbnut/work/decision-record.md`."
